# Configuration 7 -- two causal domains joined by a slow train.
#
#   Miner x4 -> MineHead ==[ Train x2, 3000 ticks ]==> Yard -> Smelter x20 -> ...
#
# A `link` is an ordinary machine whose outputs equal its inputs and whose two
# ends are different storages. Nothing new had to be invented for batch
# transport with latency; it was already expressible. Naming it only lets the
# domain analysis recognise what it is.
#
# What it buys is a boundary. Cut the two trains out of the wiring graph and it
# falls into two pieces. For the 3000 ticks a batch is in transit those pieces
# cannot influence each other at all, so each may be advanced on its own and
# the answers stitched together afterwards. That is a Room boundary, discovered
# from the graph rather than declared by a player.
#
# The train is the bottleneck on purpose: 2 x 4000 / 3000 = 2.67 ore/tick,
# against 6.67 mined and 10.0 of smelting capacity waiting at the far end.

item IronOre
item IronPlate

blueprint RailNetwork {
    source  Miner x4    { produces 100 IronOre every 60 ticks }
    storage MineHead    { capacity 20000  policy round_robin }

    link    Train x2    { moves 4000 IronOre takes 3000 ticks }

    storage Yard        { capacity 20000  policy round_robin }
    process Smelter x20 { consumes 10 IronOre takes 20 ticks produces 10 IronPlate }
    storage PlateBay    { capacity 5000 }
    sink    Shipping    { consumes 500 IronPlate every 100 ticks }

    wire Miner -> MineHead -> Train -> Yard -> Smelter -> PlateBay -> Shipping
}

deploy 1 x RailNetwork
